Nothing has changed on #67, so this run made no change and the issue is waiting until 2026-11-24T00:00Z.

- **The push that started this run** (9888ed0..5703e50) only adds a line from the nightly scan to `PROPOSALS.md`. It has nothing to do with this issue.
- **The base image hasn't moved.** `debian:trixie-slim` still points to the same digest (`sha256:a72b4433`, last updated on Docker Hub 2026-11-05), which still ships zlib1g `1+b1`.
- **The nightly is still red.** Its report of 9888ed0 still fails the policy on one finding only, CVE-2026-85091 on that digest's zlib1g.
- **The backport, PR #70, is still open**, so there is no patch tag to cut on release/0.1 yet.

The checkpoint push reported "2 files changed, 312 insertions" even though the checkout was clean when this run started. I didn't check which files those are. They're on `looper/llmproxy-67` only, not main.

The next run checks the digest again. When a new digest carries zlib1g `1+deb13u1`, it moves `Dockerfile:7` and the image-base pin to it, lands, and closes the issue once the nightly is clean. Once PR #70 merges, it tags v0.1.7 on release/0.1 (or the next free patch number). Jody decided there will be no exception.
